PUBLIC RESPONSE: {B. It contributes to the defense against the broad spectrum of powdery mildew pathogens}

The RPW8 locus (including its HR4 homolog) is a well-characterized contributor to broad-spectrum resistance against powdery-mildew fungi in Arabidopsis. The other choices either refer to proteins or localization patterns that belong to different defense components (ADF3, EHM-targeted RPW8.2, PAD4 interactors) or invert regulatory relationships, making them inconsistent with published data on HR4.

(The answer is reached solely from prior biological knowledge of the RPW8/HR family; no external retrieval was performed.)

